 "notes": "Fig.5 solid curve (this work, Eot-Wash ISL torsion balance, Ref[1]=Kapner et al hep-ph/0611184), 68% CL. Plotted y=(g_P^n)^2/(4*pi*hbar*c) vs mc^2 [meV] for the gamma5 pseudoscalar-neutron coupling from simultaneous two-pseudoscalar (k=3) exchange (Eq.19-21). Converted: g_an = sqrt(4*pi*y); x mass = mc2[meV]*1e-3 eV. The gamma5 Yukawa coupling g_P^n equals the canonical dimensionless g_an (integrating (g_an/2m_n) d_mu a Nbar gamma^mu gamma5 N by parts gives g_an a Nbar i gamma5 N), so no 2m_N factor applies. Solid=this work headline; dashed curve=Ref[14] Hoyle2004 (not reported); red dotted line=SN1987a. Vector data recovered from e-print 2ps_fac5.eps via GRAF tick calibration (x decades at 4.280..15.440 cm=0.001..10 meV; y decades at 2.948..12.538 cm=1e-8..1e-2). Flat g_an~5.6e-4 at low mass. Not a DM search: density-independent lab bound.",
